    "description": {
      "value": "You tear open the ground then slam it shut. The target creature takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage with a Reflex save.\n\nCritical Success: The target is unaffected.\nSuccess: The target takes half damage.\nFailure: The target takes full damage, is flat-footed, and takes a -10-foot circumstance penalty to Speed.\nCritical Failure: The target takes double damage and is flat-footed and immobilized. It can attempt to Escape against your spell DC. If it doesn't Escape, the target takes an additional 2d6 bludgeoning damage when the spell ends."
    },
    "higher_level_description": {
      "value": "Heightened (+1): Increase the initial damage and additional damage by 2d6."
    },
